### 1. the predicate over the POSITIVE CONTROL (every leg green, met=True)
    bind=1 sealed=1 code=1 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=3/3 sealedruns=3/3 coderuns=3/3 envnames=3/3 hostlibs=3/3 anon=0 twopass=3/3 rehash=0 met=True
    leg=envnames  leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    leg=code      leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    leg=rehash    leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    leg=bind      leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    leg=sealed    leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    leg=twopass   leg_failed=True   (a real kill would need this False)
    -> the predicate cannot distinguish ANY of these legs from a pass.

### 2. the predicate applied to the m-ldpreload receipt, named leg 'code'
    bind=1 sealed=1 code=1 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=3/3 sealedruns=3/3 coderuns=3/3 envnames=0/3 hostlibs=3/3 anon=0 twopass=3/3 rehash=0 met=False
    summary says code=code=1  -> the CODE leg PASSED (only envnames=0/3 failed)
    leg_failed(text, 'code') = True  -> harness ok (rc=1, met=False, leg_failed=True) = True
    -> the harness would certify 'leg=code ... -> ok' for a mutant whose
       code leg passed: the leg attribution is vacuous.

